Common mistakes are:
mixing units, such as kW and hp, mm and m, or wet and dry basis moisture;
using a formula outside its stated conditions;
forgetting losses and efficiency;
treating a crop or soil as uniform when it varies;
designing irrigation without checking the water source and scheduling;
ignoring traffic, compaction and safety;
copying software output without checking;
confusing theoretical field capacity with actual field capacity;
and leaving assumptions unstated.
Students also memorise machines without understanding the process. In professional work, an unregistered person must not sign designs where the law requires a registered engineer.
